|~ What is declared under `::group`, the steps in parentheses run on
   the value in the pipe: its constructor and its refusals, each told in
   one order: the refusal and its page, which repairs the step, its
   facts, its laws. ~|

:group/construct
  |~~ The step `(pipeline)` from the quote of its pipeline. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:group/PayloadNotQuoteError
  |~~ The payload of `::group` is the quote of its pipeline, so
      `~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group` is the step `(add 1 | mul 2)`.
      ::link~(::group | doc)
  ~~|

:group/PayloadNotQuoteError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(42 | tag ::group !| [type /actualType] | eq [::group/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number])

:group/PayloadNotQuoteError/buildsTheStepOfAPipeline
  |~~ The quote of a pipeline builds the group that runs it. ~~|
  ::law~(~(add 1 | mul 2) | tag ::group | [/] | tag ::quote | eq ~((add 1 | mul 2)))

:group/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::group` prints as text that reads back as another step, or
      as none, and `:printed` is that text: an empty group prints as
      `()`, which reads as no step. A group holds one step at least, and
      `/` keeps the value as it is, `~(/) | tag ::group`.
      ::link~(::group | doc)
  ~~|

:group/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAnEmptyGroup
  |~~ An empty group prints as text that reads back as none. ~~|
  ::law~(~() | tag ::group !| [type /printed] | eq [::group/ReadBackDiffersError "()"])

:group/ReadBackDiffersError/keepsTheValueByTheWholeValue
  |~~ A group of `/` is a step that keeps the value. ~~|
  ::law~(~(/) | tag ::group | [/] | tag ::quote | eq ~((/)))
